# kagima — the names of the environment variables, and nothing else.
#
# ⚠ This file is tracked. ⚠ `.env` is not. ⚠ Copy this to `.env` and fill the values in there.
# ⚠ **Never put a value in this file, not even a fake one that looks real**
#   (.claude/rules/security.md § 6 — ⚠ a realistic placeholder is how a real one gets committed next).
# ⚠ `node .claude/tools/docs-check.mjs --only=env-example-has-no-values` fails if a value appears.
#
# ⚠ Leave every line commented out. An empty assignment (`FOO=`) reads as "set, to nothing"
#   and is worse than an absent one.

# ── Control plane ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port the HTTP + WebSocket server listens on.
# PORT=

# Secret used to sign short-lived join tokens (.claude/rules/security.md § 4).
# ⚠ Generate with a CSPRNG. ⚠ Rotating it invalidates every live room, which is acceptable.
# JOIN_TOKEN_SECRET=

# The header the caller's address is read from, when a proxy in front always overwrites it.
# ⚠ Leave it unset unless a trusted proxy is in front. ⚠ Trusting a header that anything can set
#   lets an attacker spoof the source and walk past the per-source rate limit by typing a header.
# ⚠ Unset means the socket address is used. ⚠ Behind a tunnel that makes every caller look like
#   one source, and the per-source limit collapses into the per-room one.
# TRUSTED_SOURCE_HEADER=

# ── TURN (⚠ not part of v0.1.0 — see docs/adr/) ──────────────────────────────
# ⚠ Only fill these in once the owner has decided to run a TURN relay.
# ⚠ Until then the room falls back to STUN only and some networks will not connect.
# TURN_KEY_ID=
# TURN_KEY_API_TOKEN=
